# Core Workflow

- Prefer minimal, targeted changes over broad rewrites.
- Before editing, read nearby code and preserve existing conventions.
- Never revert user-authored changes unless explicitly requested.
- After meaningful edits, run a quick verification step (`npm run build` or focused checks).

# Safety

- Avoid destructive git commands (`reset --hard`, force push) unless explicitly requested.
- If a command could delete many files, ask for confirmation first.
- Keep secrets out of code and commits (`.env`, tokens, private keys).

# Communication

- Explain changes with short rationale and impacted files.
- When blocked, report the blocker and propose the smallest next action.

# Safety

- **[STRICT] NEVER delete any files or directories without explicit user confirmation.**
- Before proposing a file deletion, you must explain **why** it is necessary and which files will be affected.
- Avoid destructive git commands (`reset --hard`, force push) unless explicitly requested.
- If a command could delete many files, ask for confirmation first.
- Keep secrets out of code and commits (`.env`, tokens, private keys).